On the shore,

8
00:00:38,660 --> 00:00:41,080
Summer has come again this year.

9
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:43,700
It's here, it's here, it's here, it's here.

10
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:52,500
A big sea, a small sea,
a sea as small as one...

11
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:55,420
Come, southern wind!

12
00:00:55,420 --> 00:00:58,500
Big bottom, small bottom,
about the size of a little bottom,

13
00:00:58,500 --> 00:00:59,960
Come, southern wind!

14
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:08,580
Come, southern wind!

15
00:01:08,580 --> 00:01:14,520
Come, southern wind!

16
00:01:17,480 --> 00:01:18,440
On the shore

17
00:01:18,440 --> 00:01:19,260
Poro-poro

18
00:01:19,260 --> 00:01:20,020
On the shore

19
00:01:20,020 --> 00:01:20,700
Poro-poro

20
00:01:20,700 --> 00:01:21,540
Poro-poro

21
00:01:21,540 --> 00:01:22,180
Poro-poro

22
00:01:22,760 --> 00:01:23,620
Splish

23
00:01:29,580 --> 00:01:32,500
Bad-ass cop Ryotsu appears!

24
00:01:58,260 --> 00:02:01,260
Eeeeeeh

25
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:06,600
It's coming

26
00:02:08,540 --> 00:02:12,700
Aaaaaah

27
00:02:15,440 --> 00:02:17,140
Aaaaaah

28
00:02:22,060 --> 00:02:24,280
You're fired up again this morning, Ryo-san.

29
00:02:25,980 --> 00:02:26,640
I'm late!

30
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:30,800
Honestly, I can't believe he
parked somewhere like this!

31
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:32,500
What kind of nerve does he have?

32
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:34,280
You're in the way, get out of here.

33
00:02:35,460 --> 00:02:36,180
Move!

34
00:02:36,180 --> 00:02:47,320
No way!

35
00:02:48,140 --> 00:02:48,840
Wait!

36
00:02:51,140 --> 00:02:53,420
Eeeeeeh

37
00:02:53,420 --> 00:02:55,720
Aaaaaah

38
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:56,340
Aaaaaah

39
00:02:56,340 --> 00:02:57,840
Aaaaaah

40
00:03:04,460 --> 00:03:07,438
The ugliest, most battered man in Kameari,

41
00:03:07,488 --> 00:03:09,760
you irresponsible caveman of a man!

42
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:14,380
You there on that bicycle, wait!
You caveman!

43
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:20,620
Hmph! You think you can
catch the great Kankichi?

44
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:24,460
Now 30 kilometers over the speed limit!

45
00:03:26,420 --> 00:03:28,840
Then 40 kilometers, 50 kilometers,

46
00:03:28,890 --> 00:03:31,740
60 kilometers, 70 kilometers, 80 kilometers!

47
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:36,540
The engine has hit the
redline at maximum revs

48
00:03:37,280 --> 00:03:39,200
Full lock, turning 90 degrees

49
00:03:45,540 --> 00:03:46,440
Totally terrible

50
00:03:47,540 --> 00:03:47,840
No

51
00:04:05,020 --> 00:04:07,840
Aaaaaah!

52
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,640
Made it just in time!

53
00:04:25,120 --> 00:04:26,880
Made it, made it!

54
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:32,560
Where there's a will, there's a way.
Phew, thank goodness.

55
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:38,080
That's not good, Ryo-san! You broke the glass again,
and the Chief's going to scold us!

56
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:44,600
Hey, Ryo-chan! I've been watering that flower every day,
and it finally bloomed!

57
00:04:45,060 --> 00:04:46,700
If you touch it again, I won't forgive you.

58
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:49,940
As noisy as ever.

59
00:04:51,240 --> 00:04:53,440
What, the Chief still hasn't come?

60
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:54,940
Tsk, that won't do.

61
00:04:56,880 --> 00:04:57,581
Honestly,

62
00:04:57,631 --> 00:05:01,240
someone in charge should always
come in thirty minutes early.

63
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:03,940
R-Ryo-san.

64
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:07,940
What's wrong with you, eek!

65
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:22,000
Chief

66
00:05:22,860 --> 00:05:24,820
Right on time again today, I see.

67
00:05:24,820 --> 00:05:26,500
Well, coming all the
way from the countryside,

68
00:05:26,500 --> 00:05:29,460
commuting two and a half hours every day,
that's impressive.

69
00:05:29,460 --> 00:05:32,420
You're truly a mirror for
all police officers, Chief.

70
00:05:32,420 --> 00:05:34,020
Bakabon

71
00:05:36,740 --> 00:05:38,760
Who cares if the alarm doesn't go off?

72
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:41,760
You didn't turn up late today,
so that's perfect.

73
00:05:41,760 --> 00:05:45,180
You slid in safely,
just one minute before the deadline.

74
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:47,200
Bakabon

75
00:05:49,260 --> 00:05:53,340
No matter how old you get,
you still act like the neighborhood bully.

76
00:05:53,340 --> 00:05:55,960
How many incident reports do you
have to write before you're satisfied?

77
00:05:55,960 --> 00:05:58,060
Are you trying to get into
the Guinness Book of Records?

78
00:05:58,060 --> 00:06:00,340
That's why no bride has ever come your way.

79
00:06:00,340 --> 00:06:03,140
Let's live our lives more steadily!

80
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:05,835
There's a song by Kiyoko
Mizumachi that I love,

81
00:06:05,885 --> 00:06:07,400
and it goes like this.

82
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:10,820
One day, one step,

83
00:06:10,870 --> 00:06:13,210
three days, three steps,

84
00:06:13,260 --> 00:06:17,600
three steps forward, two steps back.

85
00:06:17,700 --> 00:06:18,480
Bam! That's it!

86
00:06:18,700 --> 00:06:21,180
Yoi yoi yoi! The Chief's Kiyoko Mizumachi!

87
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:25,740
That's it, that's it. In life,
three steps forward, two steps back.

88
00:06:25,820 --> 00:06:28,260
Taking one step forward and
then resting is the same thing.

89
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:38,240
I was foolish to try to
teach you humility about life.

90
00:06:40,200 --> 00:06:41,600
My head hurts.

91
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:44,880
Finally, it's over.

92
00:06:45,340 --> 00:06:47,320
Every other word out of your mouth is
"idiot, idiot."

93
00:06:47,320 --> 00:06:49,800
That's the kind of thing
a fool learns by rote.

94
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:54,880
Chief.

95
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:57,360
Did you forget something?

96
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:03,480
Oh right, today is payday.

97
00:07:04,260 --> 00:07:06,900
I don't want to give it to you,
but I have no choice.

98
00:07:06,900 --> 00:07:08,040
Listen, Ryotsu.

99
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:11,500
Just because you've got money doesn't
mean you should spend it right away.

100
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:15,740
Think about the future and make sure
you spend it wisely and with a plan.

101
00:07:16,820 --> 00:07:17,220
Yes.

102
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:24,060
I can add another remote-control car!

103
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:28,600
What are you doing, Chief?

104
00:07:29,260 --> 00:07:31,540
The crystallized sweat
and tears of my whole month!

105
00:07:32,220 --> 00:07:33,850
The door and the glass,

106
00:07:33,900 --> 00:07:36,540
and the bicycle compensation too.

107
00:07:37,180 --> 00:07:38,720
Tch, what a tightwad.

108
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:41,300
Well, that's fine. With this much left,

109
00:07:41,300 --> 00:07:43,720
finally, it's Friday!

110
00:07:48,460 --> 00:07:51,160
We've come to collect
payment for the rescue.

111
00:07:52,700 --> 00:07:55,060
Oh no, the entire
shopping district has come!

112
00:07:55,720 --> 00:07:58,600
Damn it, in that case, run!

113
00:08:00,260 --> 00:08:00,640
Chief!

114
00:08:01,020 --> 00:08:03,480
Everyone! Hold Ryotsu's legs!

115
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:05,280
Y-yes!

116
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:07,540
Pay up! Pay up!

117
00:08:08,300 --> 00:08:09,680
Everyone! Let go of me!

118
00:08:11,420 --> 00:08:13,960
Well, everyone, please take these!

119
00:08:14,140 --> 00:08:14,700
Pay up!

120
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:16,880
Sorry, Ryo-san.

121
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:19,920
Game software and plum fees, 38,000 yen.

122
00:08:20,020 --> 00:08:20,960
I'll take that.

123
00:08:21,420 --> 00:08:23,400
Plum fees, 22,000 yen.

124
00:08:24,320 --> 00:08:26,840
Beer and whiskey, 28,000 yen.

125
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:28,580
Could you at least wrap it up, Kage.

126
00:08:30,260 --> 00:08:31,820
Yeah, yeah, that's eighteen thousand yen!

127
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:32,540
Here you go!

128
00:08:32,880 --> 00:08:34,160
Fishing rod, 3,000 yen!

129
00:08:34,280 --> 00:08:35,200
Seriously? For real!

130
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:36,140
Seventeen thousand yen!

131
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:37,000
Mike!

132
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,120
One hundred and fifty yen...

133
00:08:45,200 --> 00:08:47,460
H-how am I supposed to get
by this month with just this?!

134
00:08:48,100 --> 00:08:49,165
Serves you right.

135
00:08:49,215 --> 00:08:52,720
That's why I keep saying you have to live a sensible,
frugal life.

136
00:08:53,020 --> 00:08:53,760
Chief!

137
00:08:54,300 --> 00:08:55,540
You're not allowed to borrow money!

138
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:58,600
Be a man and try living
a whole month on just that!

139
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:03,860
Terai, and you too, Reiko, if you lend
Ryotsu any money, that's not allowed.

140
00:09:04,660 --> 00:09:07,240
I've got a house loan to pay off too,
you know.

141
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:11,400
It's fine.
Ryo-chan can easily get by on that much.

142
00:09:12,260 --> 00:09:14,940
That's right, I can't spoil him.
It's for Ryotsu's own good.

143
00:09:15,280 --> 00:09:17,664
Chief, don't say that. Fifty thousand,

144
00:09:17,714 --> 00:09:19,720
or even thirty thousand is fine.

145
00:09:20,120 --> 00:09:23,045
Uh, then twenty thousand

146
00:09:23,095 --> 00:09:26,300
ten thousand,
or at least just one thousand yen.

147
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:27,800
No way!

148
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:28,260
Nooo!

149
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:29,400
Weeee!

150
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:31,420
Mukkejii!

151
00:09:33,780 --> 00:09:35,420
I'm never begging anyone again, wei!

152
00:09:35,920 --> 00:09:38,020
Rather than beg these cold-hearted people,

153
00:09:38,020 --> 00:09:39,680
I'd rather starve to death!

154
00:09:40,860 --> 00:09:43,520
You said it,
so don't you forget those words.

155
00:09:44,340 --> 00:09:46,660
Don't come crying to me when you're hungry.

156
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:54,160
I'll live a grand,
elegant life on 150 yen, just you watch!

157
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:56,380
Kids' squabbling

158
00:10:32,080 --> 00:10:33,220
How should I take it, I wonder?

159
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:43,228
Ryo-chan,

160
00:10:43,278 --> 00:10:48,000
who was it that said starving to
death was better than begging for help?

161
00:10:49,780 --> 00:10:52,620
Damn, he's read my pattern.

162
00:11:02,180 --> 00:11:04,280
Hand over your bed!

163
00:11:04,760 --> 00:11:07,460
N-no way! This one's mine!

164
00:11:07,760 --> 00:11:08,140
Hand it over!

165
00:11:08,940 --> 00:11:12,040
Ryo-chan, stealing from your
big brother is seriously annoying!

166
00:11:12,660 --> 00:11:15,220
Shut up! Is there some kind of scam
written on the grains of rice or something?

167
00:11:16,620 --> 00:11:17,680
Come on, hand it over!

168
00:11:19,780 --> 00:11:21,880
Ryo-chan, stop it!

169
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:23,320
Hand it over, I said!

170
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:25,060
No way, Jimmer!

171
00:11:41,120 --> 00:11:43,040
Alright, if it's come to this, so be it.

172
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:55,280
You really go all out when it comes to food,
don't you?

173
00:12:01,820 --> 00:12:03,080
Damn it!

174
00:12:10,760 --> 00:12:11,240
Ugh!

175
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:14,540
Grr! Next time I see him,
I'll turn him into a scarf!

176
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:25,380
I'm so hungry...

177
00:12:26,360 --> 00:12:28,620
Isn't there any food around here...?

178
00:12:28,620 --> 00:12:30,940
Found some! A kagami mochi!

179
00:12:31,980 --> 00:12:34,860
There's always something to eat somewhere,
you know.

180
00:12:34,860 --> 00:12:38,320
A little spray and ponzu...

181
00:12:38,320 --> 00:12:40,000
I put in too much!

182
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:44,040
This is too sour,
so I'll add some salt to make it dry.

183
00:12:46,580 --> 00:12:49,760
I definitely overdid it.
Let's add some sugar.

184
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:54,660
Well, it'll do. This should be fine.

185
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:58,360
For the finishing touch,
season it with tonkatsu sauce.

186
00:12:58,900 --> 00:13:00,540
My mass-production hotpot is complete!

187
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:03,640
There were leftover New Year's kagami mochi.

188
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:08,140
Isn't that the mochi that
was totally covered in mold?

189
00:13:08,880 --> 00:13:09,780
You idiot.

190
00:13:09,780 --> 00:13:11,580
Mushrooms are a type of mold too, right?

191
00:13:11,580 --> 00:13:13,660
And hydrangea leaves went in there too.

192
00:13:13,660 --> 00:13:15,640
The nutritional balance is perfect.

193
00:13:16,220 --> 00:13:18,540
Eating hydrangea leaves, of all things...

194
00:13:18,880 --> 00:13:20,560
It's called "aji-sai," so

195
00:13:20,560 --> 00:13:22,080
it's bound to taste good.

196
00:13:24,640 --> 00:13:26,140
The colors are a bit off, though.

197
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:31,060
Ryo-san,

198
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:32,780
that's Reiko's...

199
00:13:32,780 --> 00:13:35,500
Color is important in cooking, you know.

200
00:13:38,200 --> 00:13:39,120
Thanks for the meal.

201
00:13:41,780 --> 00:13:43,240
Ryo-chan!

202
00:13:43,920 --> 00:13:46,420
What have you done?

203
00:13:48,560 --> 00:13:51,020
I told you never to touch it again!

204
00:13:51,020 --> 00:13:52,120
Barbarian!

205
00:13:59,340 --> 00:14:00,260
Damn it!

206
00:14:00,860 --> 00:14:03,400
You could've saved some from before,
you cheapskate.

207
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:08,560
How clumsy.

208
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:15,780
What's this?

209
00:14:21,800 --> 00:14:23,640
There! Right there!

210
00:14:24,940 --> 00:14:27,560
Isn't that Junpei and
Kappei from the tofu shop?

211
00:14:33,520 --> 00:14:34,960
Yes, yes, how about that!

212
00:14:35,560 --> 00:14:36,800
Come on, Junpei-chan!

213
00:14:37,660 --> 00:14:38,860
Come on!

214
00:14:39,480 --> 00:14:41,920
No, no, look at him go, Sho-kun.

215
00:14:42,540 --> 00:14:44,560
He's got quite a good arm, doesn't he?

216
00:14:45,800 --> 00:14:47,400
Those takoyaki look delicious.

217
00:14:47,560 --> 00:14:49,940
What do you say, Junpei?
Why don't you take me on?

218
00:14:50,720 --> 00:14:52,440
You mean you, Ryo-san?

219
00:14:53,220 --> 00:14:55,360
That's right.
One round, one game, winner takes all.

220
00:14:55,500 --> 00:14:58,400
If I win, I get these takoyaki.

221
00:14:59,700 --> 00:15:01,000
And if Ryo-san loses?

222
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:06,500
You can have whichever one you like from my collection,
whether it's a model kit or a game software.

223
00:15:07,300 --> 00:15:08,240
Model kits?

224
00:15:09,300 --> 00:15:11,560
So? Are you in, Junpei?

225
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:12,600
Yeah.

226
00:15:13,660 --> 00:15:16,900
Go for it, Kansuke-nken!
Go for it, big brother!

227
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:23,000
Sure is lively Oh, Ryo-san.

228
00:15:28,700 --> 00:15:29,340
Yes!

229
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,260
980 points.

230
00:15:32,260 --> 00:15:34,380
Not bad.

231
00:15:34,380 --> 00:15:36,380
Okay, my turn next.

232
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:40,620
Start.

233
00:15:40,620 --> 00:15:42,260
Start.

234
00:15:42,260 --> 00:15:45,880
Beni-eda, shoot!

235
00:15:49,880 --> 00:15:51,580
Aaaaaaah!

236
00:15:51,580 --> 00:15:53,140
Aaaaaaah!

237
00:15:59,060 --> 00:16:00,260
Gotcha!

238
00:16:00,260 --> 00:16:03,780
Face shot!

239
00:16:04,780 --> 00:16:06,480
Aaaaaaah!

240
00:16:06,480 --> 00:16:07,960
Aaaaaaah!

241
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:21,880
How about that?

242
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:23,360
I lost.

243
00:16:23,360 --> 00:16:25,940
We should've quit while we were ahead,
big brother.

244
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:29,020
As promised, I'm taking the takoyaki.

245
00:16:34,780 --> 00:16:35,300
Aaaaaah!

246
00:16:35,300 --> 00:16:37,640
Aaaaaah!

247
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:38,340
Aaaaaah!

248
00:16:38,340 --> 00:16:39,600
Aaaaaah!

249
00:16:39,600 --> 00:16:42,220
Aaaaaah!

250
00:16:42,220 --> 00:16:43,600
Aaaaaah!

251
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:44,700
Aaaaaaah!

252
00:16:44,700 --> 00:16:45,720
Aaaaaaah!

253
00:16:45,720 --> 00:16:46,540
Aaaaaaah!

254
00:16:46,540 --> 00:16:47,160
Aaaaaaah!

255
00:16:47,160 --> 00:16:47,240
Aaaaaaah!

256
00:16:47,240 --> 00:16:47,720
Aaaaaaah!

257
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:48,120
Aaaaaaah!

258
00:16:48,120 --> 00:16:48,980
Aaaaaaah!

259
00:16:48,980 --> 00:16:49,060
Aaaaaaah!

260
00:16:49,060 --> 00:16:49,460
Aaaaaaah!

261
00:16:49,460 --> 00:16:49,860
Aaaaaaah!

262
00:16:49,860 --> 00:16:51,960
Ryo-san! Catch him for us!

263
00:16:52,380 --> 00:16:54,720
Leave it to me! Stop right there!

264
00:16:59,760 --> 00:17:01,640
Stop!

265
00:17:03,340 --> 00:17:04,100
Uh-oh!

266
00:17:12,700 --> 00:17:13,840
Watch out, you'll get hit by a bike!

267
00:17:15,380 --> 00:17:18,040
Ultra Power Turbo, activate!

268
00:17:31,260 --> 00:17:33,660
Yes! We chased him down on bicycles!

269
00:17:34,120 --> 00:17:35,260
There's no way we'll catch up!

270
00:17:36,140 --> 00:17:37,940
Just because he's ahead a little,
I'm not getting caught!

271
00:17:50,860 --> 00:17:51,760
Aaaaaah!

272
00:17:54,900 --> 00:17:57,900
No way, seriously!
We're letting him get away!

273
00:17:59,020 --> 00:18:00,360
Aaaaaah!

274
00:18:13,260 --> 00:18:16,260
You bastard! Alright, we'll cut him off!

275
00:18:17,050 --> 00:18:20,260
Missile Jump!

276
00:18:20,260 --> 00:18:43,540
!

277
00:18:43,540 --> 00:18:43,920
Shortcut!

278
00:18:50,800 --> 00:18:52,600
Damn! I took the wrong road!

279
00:18:56,100 --> 00:18:57,820
Pyo-san, what are you doing!

280
00:18:58,300 --> 00:19:00,360
Zumakkōbu in progress!

281
00:19:09,300 --> 00:19:10,880
I'm heading out!

282
00:19:15,100 --> 00:19:16,220
Mm...

283
00:19:25,880 --> 00:19:27,340
What are you doing?

284
00:19:27,340 --> 00:19:29,800
What are we chasing?

285
00:19:34,580 --> 00:19:35,420
Jabu!

286
00:19:38,800 --> 00:19:39,960
Ugh, we caught up!

287
00:19:41,440 --> 00:19:43,960
They're still coming after us! Hurry, hurry!

288
00:19:44,080 --> 00:19:45,420
What a persistent bunch.

289
00:19:49,920 --> 00:19:52,100
Don't underestimate the base!

290
00:20:00,960 --> 00:20:02,440
They're catching up to us
at 80 kilometers an hour?!

291
00:20:02,440 --> 00:20:04,080
Hurry!

292
00:20:12,540 --> 00:20:14,320
Get out of the way, you stupid dog!

293
00:20:31,660 --> 00:20:32,340
Yes!

294
00:20:32,360 --> 00:20:33,300
Looks like he finally gave up.

295
00:20:33,820 --> 00:20:34,620
No way!

296
00:20:38,840 --> 00:20:40,520
Hey, you bastard, wait!

297
00:20:42,520 --> 00:21:09,440
!

298
00:21:11,540 --> 00:21:12,920
He's not following us anymore.

299
00:21:13,540 --> 00:21:14,880
We did it, Ken-chan!

300
00:21:14,880 --> 00:21:16,080
How about that!

301
00:21:25,760 --> 00:21:27,520
Oh no, it's a dead end!

302
00:21:30,540 --> 00:21:53,620
!

303
00:21:54,620 --> 00:21:55,400
Hahaha!

304
00:21:55,400 --> 00:21:57,080
You bastard!

305
00:21:57,760 --> 00:22:00,380
Sorry, I'll never do it again, I promise.

306
00:22:02,040 --> 00:22:03,760
Give back the takoyaki!

307
00:22:05,980 --> 00:22:08,140
It's takoyaki, takoyaki!

308
00:22:08,140 --> 00:22:10,000
Give me back my takoyaki, damn it!

309
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:20,820
You did it, Ryo-chan.

310
00:22:21,660 --> 00:22:25,000
Your first criminal study in eight years,
congratulations!

311
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:28,700
Well, I've been keeping my
claws hidden for a while.

312
00:22:29,440 --> 00:22:31,600
A clever hawk hides its claws, right?

313
00:22:31,860 --> 00:22:33,660
It doesn't really suit you, Ryo-chan.

314
00:22:33,660 --> 00:22:35,200
Ryo-san!

315
00:22:35,920 --> 00:22:37,080
Junpei.

316
00:22:37,760 --> 00:22:39,140
Is your leg all better now?

317
00:22:40,040 --> 00:22:41,960
This is nothing serious, man.

318
00:22:41,960 --> 00:22:45,540
Ryo-san,
I'm definitely winning this game next time!

319
00:22:46,140 --> 00:22:49,480
Yeah, yeah,
you'd better keep practicing, Junpei!

320
00:22:51,180 --> 00:22:54,020
Come to think of it,
we haven't eaten anything yet.

321
00:22:54,900 --> 00:22:59,800
Right, I heard that driver was
a notorious traffic offender.

322
00:23:00,480 --> 00:23:04,400
Could this be a special
commendation with a cash award?

323
00:23:04,400 --> 00:23:08,420
A cash award! This'll save us this month!

324
00:23:08,420 --> 00:23:10,400
Yo, Suwairu...

325
00:23:14,920 --> 00:23:17,300
Yes, we've arrested a
vicious hit-and-run driver.

326
00:23:17,300 --> 00:23:19,180
Kameari's top cop.

327
00:23:19,180 --> 00:23:21,080
If you mean Senior Officer Kankichi Ryotsu,

328
00:23:21,080 --> 00:23:22,440
he's right here.

329
00:23:25,420 --> 00:23:27,580
You're giving me the
cash commendation, right?

330
00:23:27,580 --> 00:23:29,800
Idiot!

331
00:23:32,300 --> 00:23:33,480
Look outside.

332
00:23:38,460 --> 00:23:39,120
Ryotsu!

333
00:23:39,120 --> 00:23:43,040
I hear you've caused trouble
for the neighbors again.

334
00:23:43,040 --> 00:23:46,640
You'll pay for the damages
out of next month's salary.

335
00:23:47,700 --> 00:23:48,580
No way...

336
00:23:50,040 --> 00:23:51,760
Please, have mercy.

337
00:23:51,760 --> 00:23:53,000
Smooch!

338
00:24:05,680 --> 00:24:09,080
A new rookie cop is coming to
the Kameari Park police box.

339
00:24:09,080 --> 00:24:12,520
Apparently he's the only son
of the rich Nakagawa zaibatsu.

340
00:24:12,520 --> 00:24:16,180
Hmph, like some pampered rich
kid could hack it as a cop.

341
00:24:17,660 --> 00:24:20,400
Next time, the rookie cop who came from the sky,
see you then.

342
00:24:31,280 --> 00:24:35,660
Let's always keep smiling.

343
00:24:35,660 --> 00:24:39,860
Even when something outrageous happens,

344
00:24:39,860 --> 00:24:44,380
keep smiling cutely, okay?

345
00:24:44,380 --> 00:24:49,600
Just step out with a casual face,
that's all.

346
00:24:49,600 --> 00:24:56,500
Hey, smile for me. It's not your fault.

347
00:24:57,780 --> 00:25:04,740
Hey, smile for me,
just like you were a moment ago.

348
00:25:04,740 --> 00:25:15,640
Keep smiling always, because a woman playing
at being all dark and gloomy isn't pretty.

349
00:25:15,640 --> 00:25:20,340
You should smile right away.

350
00:25:21,580 --> 00:25:24,820
Unless you're a kid, that is.

